6ae185d0d24a85ae5c54ae6f","name":"RATatouille: Today's Special: Impersonating Companies in Korea, Payments in Cryptocurrency","description":"Infrastructure tracking related to ValleyRAT led to the discovery of multiple fraudulent websites impersonating legitimate Korean companies including Doosan Robotics and Cheonjeong. These sites used authentic corporate logos, videos, and descriptions to appear legitimate while offering features like invitation-code registration, VIP memberships, and cryptocurrency deposit\/withdrawal functions. Online chat support provided instructions for USDT payments via TRON wallet addresses, requiring users to submit transaction screenshots. Analysis revealed TRON wallet addresses with significant transaction volumes, including one wallet that received approximately 13 million USDT cumulatively. Infrastructure analysis starting from ValleyRAT C2 IP address 14.128.53[.]155 identified 12 potentially associated domains. However, no direct operational connection has been confirmed between ValleyRAT malware operations and these fraudulent websites or cryptocurrency wallets.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-27T05:00:26.385000","created":"2026-10-28T05:19:12.074000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4462640301,"indicator":"chumchurumcc.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-28T05:19:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4549690860,"indicator":"chumchurumc.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-28T05:19:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4549690859,"indicator":"chumchurum.xyz","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-28T05:19:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4549690856,"indicator":"chumchurum.org","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-28T05:19:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4549690858,"indicator":"chumchuru.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-28T05:19:12","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["usdt","cryptocurrency fraud","valleyrat","phishing websites","RATatouille"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["ValleyRAT"],"attack_ids":["T1566","T1583.006","T1585.001","T1036.005","T1588.002","T1589.002","T1598","T1185","T1204","T1027","T1071.001","T1583.001","T1102","T1608.001"],"references":["https:\/\/asec.ahnlab.com\/en\/96151\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ae14ab2a51c8b2b96924ba2","name":"Omegatech Is Disrupted, and the Pressure on Bulletproof Hosting Keeps Building","description":"The FBI seized virtualine[.]net on October 27, 2026, under Operation Omegaline, targeting Virtualine Technologies, which operated as Omegatech (AS202412). This bulletproof hosting provider emerged in February 2026 after infrastructure shifted from Railnet LLC (AS214943). Bulletproof hosting providers rent servers to cybercriminals while ignoring abuse complaints, enabling phishing, malware, and ransomware operations. Over the past year, 50 such providers lost their autonomous system numbers due to law enforcement action, sanctions, or strategic abandonment. Despite seizures, operators quickly rebrand and acquire new ASNs within days, moving malicious IP ranges to continue operations. Recent enforcement actions include Dutch seizure of THE.Hosting servers, US charges against Russian nationals, and EU sanctions against Media Land. The investigation involved FBI Washington Field Office, Germany's Polizei Hessen, Netherlands' Politie Midden-Nederland, UK's National Crime Agency, and private partners.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-27T01:01:29.310000","created":"2026-10-28T01:06:58.531000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":3237199648,"indicator":"virtualine.net","type":"domain","created